Rules
- Working hours are configurable.
- 6 hours, 8 hours, 10 hours, etc. are all possible.
- Different shifts may have different working hours.
- Break/lunch is considered part of the configured working period.
- No separate lunch-break configuration is required.
- Flexible employee start/end time is not required.
- Grace is configurable per shift.
- Grace may be 5, 10, 15 minutes, or another configured value if required.
- Actual late minutes are preserved.
- Grace only determines whether the employee is considered late/early.
- Grace does not subtract the grace period from the actual attendance duration.

Example
Shift: 08:00 - 16:00
Grace In: 10 minutes

Actual IN: 08:12

Late Minutes = 12
Late Status = Yes

NOT:
Late Minutes = 2

Similarly:
Shift: 08:00 - 16:00
Grace Out: 10 minutes

Actual OUT: 15:48

Early Out Minutes = 12
Early Out Status = Yes

Roster is not mandatory.
Roster can be fixed or rotating.
Roster can be employee-specific.
One roster pattern can be used by multiple employees.
Supervisor cannot modify a published roster.

