1. Everything is configurable/data-driven.
2. Shift duration is configurable.
3. Different shifts can have different working hours.
4. Break/lunch is included in working hours.
5. Shift grace-in and grace-out are configurable.
6. Actual late/early minutes are preserved; grace only affects status.
7. Roster is optional.
8. Employees can have general/fixed duty without a roster.
9. Employees can have individual rotating rosters.
10. A roster pattern can be assigned to multiple employees.
11. Published rosters cannot be changed by supervisors.
12. Biometric machines provide punches without IN/OUT type.
13. System determines IN/OUT based on duty and shift time.
14. Cross-midnight shifts are supported.
15. One processed attendance result per employee per duty date.
16. Attendance cannot be manually edited.
17. Missing punches use an employee correction application.
18. Attendance correction is limited to 5 requests per employee per month.
19. Weekend can be any day.
20. Weekend can be employee-specific or roster-based.
21. Holidays can be configured for any date.
22. Holiday work is treated as overtime.
23. Leave groups are configurable.
24. Leave entitlement is configurable by year/policy.
25. Casual leave can carry forward.
26. Maternity leave currently supports 180 lifetime days.
27. Paternity leave currently supports 90 lifetime days.
28. Leave year and payroll period are independent.
29. Payroll cycle can have arbitrary start/end periods.
30. Payroll cycle can be used by multiple employees.
31. Employees can have individual payroll-cycle assignments.
32. Absent days are non-payable.
33. Leave may be paid or unpaid according to policy.
34. Leave approval is employee submission → manager approval.
35. Manager can return an application for editing.
36. Employee can edit and resubmit returned applications.
37. HR cannot bypass approval.
38. Approved leave cannot be cancelled by employee.
39. Payroll locks after approval/finalization.
40. Payslip is generated from finalized payroll.
41. Historical payroll must remain auditable.
42. Reports should cover employee, attendance, roster, leave and payroll.
